From: B Honey <9922368+Mhsbrian@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 08:56:40 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 2/7] nvk: advertise two queues in the graphics queue family

Android's HWUI (frameworks/base/libs/hwui/renderthread/VulkanManager.cpp)
picks the first queue family with VK_QUEUE_GRAPHICS_BIT, aborts if its
queueCount is below 2, and creates two queues there: one for the render
thread and one for AHardwareBuffer uploads. With one graphics queue, every
app process that renders its UI with Skia on Vulkan aborts at startup.

nvk_queue_create() already gives each queue its own channel, push stream,
draw constant buffer and queue state, and the transfer family has always
had two queues, so this only raises the count. Both graphics queues use
the device's shader local memory area (dev->slm), which is sized for the
whole GPU.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/nouveau/vulkan/nvk_physical_device.c | 6 +++++-
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/nouveau/vulkan/nvk_physical_device.c b/src/nouveau/vulkan/nvk_physical_device.c
index 71242e72cd9..9224e083bab 100644
--- a/src/nouveau/vulkan/nvk_physical_device.c
+++ b/src/nouveau/vulkan/nvk_physical_device.c
@@ -1670,12 +1670,16 @@ nvk_create_drm_physical_device(struct vk_instance *_instance,
    assert(pdev->mem_heap_count <= ARRAY_SIZE(pdev->mem_heaps));
    assert(pdev->mem_type_count <= ARRAY_SIZE(pdev->mem_types));
 
+   /* Android's HWUI creates two queues in the first graphics family, one for
+    * the render thread and one for AHardwareBuffer uploads, and aborts if
+    * that family has fewer.  Each queue gets its own channel.
+    */
    pdev->queue_families[pdev->queue_family_count++] = (struct nvk_queue_family) {
       .queue_flags = VK_QUEUE_GRAPHICS_BIT |
                      VK_QUEUE_COMPUTE_BIT |
                      VK_QUEUE_TRANSFER_BIT |
                      VK_QUEUE_SPARSE_BINDING_BIT,
-      .queue_count = 1,
+      .queue_count = 2,
    };
    if (pdev->info.has_transfer_queue) {
       pdev->queue_families[pdev->queue_family_count++] = (struct nvk_queue_family) {
